      "title": "Beat Frequency (f_beat)",
      "language": "en",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "e2c5c034-041b-5340-9823-5e3c8c88a07c",
          "pdf_from": 158,
          "pdf_to": 158,
          "note": "Beat Frequency (f_beat): a main subheading of 7.9 Beats, its own page (owner 2026-11-04); PDF 158-158."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The difference between the frequencies of the two waves is termed as beat frequency f_beat. The time interval between the two successive loud sound is T = t₂ − t₁. Therefore,"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "f_{\\text{beat}} = \\frac{1}{T}",
            "text_alt": "f_beat = 1/T"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
